1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
Your 4WD or AWD binding up

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:03,000
in tight turns? Not your tires.

3
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:04,700
A shudder, hop, or bind

4
00:00:04,700 --> 00:00:06,400
in a slow, tight turn —

5
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,000
parking lot, driveway, dry pavement.

6
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:09,800
That points to your transfer case

7
00:00:09,800 --> 00:00:11,700
or center differential —

8
00:00:11,700 --> 00:00:14,000
lets all 4 wheels travel different paths.

9
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Old or low transfer case fluid

10
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:17,900
can make binding worse —

11
00:00:17,900 --> 00:00:20,000
and wears the drivetrain faster.

12
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,300
One clue is not a diagnosis —

13
00:00:22,300 --> 00:00:24,300
worth having the fluid checked

14
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:26,000
before it's a bigger repair.

15
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:31,000
Stop by and we'll take a look — Nick's Tire and Auto, on Euclid Avenue.
